independently extractable <code>raw_part1..4.tar</code> volumes by sample-ID range. Each sample carries <b>32 Zernike-coefficient labels</b> (Noll convention, Z4\u2013Z35, in waves), together with the locked train/val/test split (6,674/834/835).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>raw_part1..4.tar</code> - 16,686 raw intensity PNGs, each part independently extractable</li>\n<li><code>cached.tar</code> / <code>cached_test_only.tar</code> - preprocessed <code>.pt</code> samples (lightweight entry point: test split only)</li>\n<li><code>weights_seed{0,1,2}.pth</code> - best SDPNet baseline checkpoints (siamese ResNet-18 encoder, 13.0M parameters, three random seeds)</li>\n<li><code>label.txt</code>, <code>train/val/test_ids.txt</code> - 32 Zernike coefficients per sample and the locked split</li>\n<li><code>zscore_params.npz</code>, <code>global_minmax.npz</code> - normalization parameters</li>\n<li><code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code>, <code>manifest.json</code> - integrity checksums and manifest</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Caliber notes (must-read):</b> all counts are in camera count units with uncalibrated sensor gain, so absolute photon numbers cannot be converted directly; the measured-template protocol is per-frame median background subtraction, centroid centering, 256\u00d7256 ROI, 4\u00d74 binning; RMSE values are per-coefficient (element-wise) over the 32 modes - wavefront RMS is the quadratic sum over modes (\u2248\u221a32\u00d7 larger).</p>\n<p><b>Integrity:</b> verify after download with <code>sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Funding:</b> National Key Research and Development Program of China (2024YFF1400500).</p>\n<p><b>Contact:</b> corresponding author: jijieliu@mail.ustc.edu.cn</p>\n<p><b>Code availability:</b> the key code is withheld in compliance with confidentiality requirements and is not distributed with this dataset; it is available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request.</p>", "funding": "National Key Research and Development Program of China (2024YF